Send the VP9 compressed-header probability updates.

The stateless VP9 control for the compressed header carries the probability
deltas from that header, plus the transform mode. Zero means "leave this
probability alone". Apple's decoder does not parse the compressed header
itself. Without the control it keeps the default probabilities and a 4x4
transform mode. Profile 0 still finishes a frame. Profile 2's 10-bit
keyframe updates those probabilities (its transform mode is 16x16, not
4x4), the firmware loses the bitstream, and the mailbox comes back as
status 8.

Chromium's parser stops at the uncompressed header, so the delegate reads
the compressed header from the frame bytes the same way the VA-API shim
does. The values are the inv_map deltas, not the absolute probabilities:
the kernel applies the remap itself. reference_mode comes from that same
parse. Drivers that do not expose the control are left alone.

Any stateless VP9 decoder that cannot parse the compressed header needs
this. It is not an Apple-only change.

